#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:38
msgid "OAuth 2.0 Credentials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:40
msgid ""
"|morpheus| supports storage of credential sets for retrieving temporary "
"access tokens, through OAuth 2.0, and using the tokens to access some "
"resource. These credential sets can be used with REST-type Option Lists "
"to retrieve information behind this type of authentication wall. Once "
"stored, the credential can be used with as many Option Lists as needed "
"and potentially in other areas of the product in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:42
msgid ""
"To create a new credential set, click :guilabel:`+ ADD` and then select "
"\"OAuth 2.0\". Complete the following, not all fields are present or "
"required in every context:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:44
msgid ""
"**CREDENTIAL STORE:** Select \"Internal\" or an integrated external "
"Cypher store (if any). See the next section for instructions on standing "
"up and integrating with an external Cypher store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:48
msgid "**GRANT TYPE:** Client Credentials or Password Credentials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:49
msgid "**ACCESS TOKEN URL:** The authorization server's token endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:50
msgid "**CLIENT ID:** The client ID for an app registered with the target service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:51
msgid ""
"**CLIENT SECRET:** The client secret, often needed when requesting access"
" outside the context of a specific user"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:52
msgid ""
"**USERNAME:** (Only present with \"Password Credentials\" Grant Type) The"
" username for a user with target data access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:53
msgid ""
"**PASSWORD:** (Only present with \"Password Credentials\" Grant Type) The"
" password for the user indicated above"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:54
msgid "**SCOPE:** The scope of access requested to the target resource"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:55
msgid ""
"**CLIENT AUTHENTICATION:** \"Send as basic auth header\" or \"Send client"
" credentials in body\" - Indicates how |morpheus| should issue the token "
"received in requests to the target resource"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:57
msgid "Once done, click :guilabel:`ADD CREDENTIALS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:59
msgid ""
"With the OAuth 2.0 credential set stored, they can be set on REST-type "
"Option Lists to source data from behind a compatible authentication wall."
" With a REST-type Option List open (|LibOptOpt|), click the CREDENTIALS "
"dropdown and select the credential set you've created. Alternatively, you"
" can add a credential set directly in the add/edit Option List modal if "
"needed. Option Lists can be associated with Select List or Typeahead-type"
" Inputs and applied to Layouts, Instance Types, Workflows, and more to "
"allow for customization at provision or Workflow execution time. "
"Additional details on creating Option Lists can be found in the Library "
"section of |morpheus| docs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:70
msgid "Integrating Hashicorp Vault"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:72
msgid ""
"The Hashicorp Vault integration is not included with |morpheus| by "
"default. Download the plugin from |morpheus| `Exchange "
"<https://share.morpheusdata.com/>`_ and add the plugin to |morpheus| "
"through the `Plugins "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/administration/integrations/integrations.html#plugins>`_"
" section. This allows users to store credential sets completely outside "
"of |morpheus| and in Hashicorp Vault, which may be required by your "
"organization's IT policies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:74
#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:78
#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:182
#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:193
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:74
msgid ""
"The plugin space is universal and not specific to Tenants. If Subtenant "
"users have access to |AdmIntPlu|, any integrated plugins will be "
"available in all Tenants across the appliance. In most cases, it makes "
"sense to restrict access to this section from Subtenant users through the"
" associated Tenant Role. Instead integrate plugins from the Primary "
"Tenant and expose them to various Subtenants as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:76
msgid ""
"Once downloaded, plugins are added to |morpheus| in |AdmIntPlu|. Simply "
"browse your local filesystem for the JAR file downloaded from |morpheus| "
"Exchange and its capabilities will immediately be added to the appliance."
" After adding the plugin, configure access for the plugin to your Vault "
"server. Do this by clicking the Edit (pencil) button in the row for the "
"Vault plugin. Supply a URL for your Vault server and an access token, "
"then save your changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:78
msgid ""
"When creating a Vault integration, it's recommended that you use a long-"
"lived token. If the token suddenly becomes invalid, |morpheus| will be "
"unable to write new credential sets to Vault and will be unable to edit "
"or delete any existing ones. Additionally, you won't be able to use "
"Vault-stored credential sets elsewhere in |morpheus|, such as when "
"creating new Cloud integrations or populating REST-based Option Lists "
"which require authentication. Should this happen, simply obtain a new "
"token, edit the Vault integration, update the token, and save your "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:80
msgid ""
"With the plugin added, a new integration type will appear in |InfTruInt|."
" Click :guilabel:`+ ADD`, then \"Hashicorp Vault Credentials\" to get "
"started. The fields in the list below are available for configuration but"
" it's possible that no configuration will be necessary. If you do not "
"enter a new API URL and TOKEN value, these are taken from the plugin "
"configuration set a moment ago. Similarly, The Vault Secret Engine and "
"Secret Path can be left at default values (or empty) if those values are "
"acceptable. If you need to override the defaults or the URL/token set on "
"the plugin, you may do so here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:82
msgid "**NAME:** A friendly name for the Vault integration in |morpheus|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:83
msgid ""
"**ENABLED:** When marked, this Vault integration will be available to "
"have credentials written to it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:84
msgid "**API URL:** The URL for the Vault server (ex. http://xx.xx.xx.xx:8200)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:85
msgid "**TOKEN:** A valid API token for the server (see note below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:86
msgid ""
"**HASHICORP VAULT SECRET ENGINE:** Select KV Engine version 1 or 2, "
"additional engines may be available in the future"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:87
msgid ""
"**ENGINE MOUNT:** If desired, enter a custom engine mount. By default, if"
" left empty, credentials are written to the \"secret/\" engine mount"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:88
msgid ""
"**SECRET PATH:** If desired, enter a custom path and |morpheus| will "
"write new credential sets to that path. By default, if left empty, new "
"credentials are written to \"morpheus-credentials/\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:90
msgid "When done, click :guilabel:`SAVE CHANGES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:92
msgid ""
"With the above process finished, this Vault integration will be available"
" as a storage target when creating new credential sets. In |InfTruCre|, "
"after clicking :guilabel:`+ ADD` and selecting the type of credential set"
" to add, select the new Vault integration in the CREDENTIAL STORE field "
"(default selection is \"Internal\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:103
msgid "Installing and Integrating an External Cypher Appliance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:105
msgid ""
"The external Cypher appliance runs on a small separate VM and supports a "
"variety of base OS distributions. Credentials are securely passed to the "
"external appliance and can be retrieved and consumed in specific places "
"within |morpheus| UI. The download URL for the installer can be retrieved"
" from |morpheus| `Hub <https://app.morpheushub.com/>`_, replace the "
"placeholder URL in the instructions below with the correct URL for the "
"latest version of the Cypher appliance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:107
msgid ""
"Begin by provisioning and updating the VM for the Cypher appliance. Then,"
" download the installer. The following steps go through the installation "
"process on Ubuntu but, as mentioned in the previous paragraph, many "
"popular distributions are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:109
msgid ""
"# An example URL is shown below, find the URL for the latest version and "
"for the correct distro at |morpheus| Hub\n"
"wget https://downloads.morpheusdata.com/path/to/morpheus-"
"cypher_$version_amd64.deb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:114
msgid "Next, install and reconfigure the package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/keypairs_certificates/keypairs_certs.rst:116
msgid ""
"sudo dpkg -i morpheus-cypher_$version_amd64.deb\n"
"sudo morpheus-cypher-ctl reconfigure"
msgstr ""

